From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:56:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: worker blueprints and policy-driven task dispatch

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Enable reusable worker blueprints, policy-driven dispatch, and read-only worker observation
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 0004-disable-hosted-and-promotional-features.patch, 0006-provider-allowlist-and-openrouter-endpoint.patch
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 0008-worker-blueprints-and-policy-driven-dispatch.patch

Patch intent:
Add a worker blueprint system that lets a jcode user define reusable,
specialized subagent roles in Markdown. Each blueprint supplies durable
role instructions, model, effort, enabled-tools, disabled-tools, communication
policy, and timeout. At runtime, every valid blueprint generates a
coordinator-visible tool named `swarm_<id>` that spawns a blueprint-backed
worker, waits for completion, and returns a compact summary with paginated
follow-up reads. Optional inline input-schema and output-schema front matter
supplies compiled JSON Schema contracts. Bound oversized tool output when an
explicit blueprint policy enables it and save withheld results for authorized
bounded, read-only extraction.

Add configurable coordinator policy for task dispatch, persistent retry and
assistance counters, and a hard cap on runtime check failures. Support
bounded nested assistance, same-session handback, and exact-input native
extraction. Freeze worker and extractor snapshots, enforce canonical SDK
permissions, and support coordinator-authorized check timeouts and bounded
text pagination. Allow coordinator-authorized exact external file grants,
bind canonical identities across replay, and exclude grants from assistance.
Show readable dispatch worker names in TUI swarm and tool messages, optionally
open auto-closing read-only TUI observer panes for dispatch and bounded
extract workers, and clean up finished and blocked workers when turns end.

Why it exists:
Coordinates reusable, token-efficient worker roles with schema-validated
contracts, bounded tool output, and policy-driven task dispatch without
relying on prompts alone. Exact-file grants allow explicitly authorized work
outside the workspace without broadening workspace-relative path scopes.
Read-only TUI observer panes surface live assistant output, tool intents, and
code diffs for dispatch and output-guard extract workers without granting
session control, stealing focus, or leaving finished workers resident.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-base/src/worker_blueprint.rs, hooks.rs, terminal_launch.rs and
config/, crates/jcode-config-types/src/delegation.rs and lib.rs,
crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/blueprint.rs, check.rs, extraction_scope.rs,
and mod.rs, agent turn streaming and execution, server/dispatcher/,
dispatch_observer.rs, extraction_handler.rs, extraction_operation.rs,
internal_command.rs, headless.rs, swarm.rs, client_lifecycle.rs, and
client_session.rs, crates/jcode-terminal-launch/src/lib.rs,
src/cli/tui_launch.rs, src/main.rs, crates/jcode-tui/src/tui/app/replay.rs,
run_shell.rs, remote_diff.rs, info_widget_swarm_gallery.rs, ui_messages.rs,
ui_prepare.rs, and ui_status.rs.

Update guidance:
Preserve blueprint front-matter validation, runtime policy registration across
spawn/reload/resume, bounded worker output with authorized read-only extraction,
task dispatch lifecycle and check caps, exact external file grant confinement
and canonical replay checks, and TUI worker label rendering. Keep observer
panes default-off, one-way, bounded, read-only, and independent of worker
lifecycle, rendering live TUI events and inline file diffs and closing cleanly
when the worker finishes or blocks. Carry the initiating client's terminal
context into dispatch and extract turns, falling back to headless execution
when unfocused panes cannot be guaranteed. Clean up finished and blocked
workers from live server memory and swarm state when turns end while keeping
persisted session files and operation records intact. Report malformed and SDK
tool outcomes as well as local outcomes. On Herdr launch failure, attempt to
close only the pane identified by the split response. On session restore or
clear, revoke old internal command capabilities, bind the new session
principal, and retain admitted extraction identities and worker policy without
broadening access. Fail closed if policy restoration fails.

